          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal words conventionally and directly present Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Their later characterization as a lie concerns sincerity, not their strong avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"later_1\",\"quotation\":\"«Je vous aime», которое было ложь и еще хуже чем ложь\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.8,\"reason\":\"The expression occurs after Pierre and Hélène have publicly been treated as engaged and Pierre is holding the hand of his fiancée. His recollection that this is what must be said 'in these cases' makes the avowal a socially expected affirmation of the prospective marital bond, rather than an unrelated report of feeling. Nevertheless, the engagement has already been declared by others, and the focal words neither formulate a distinct proposal nor specify obligations, so their undertaking force is moderate rather than dominant.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты и смотрел на ее поднимающуюся и опускающуюся прекрасную грудь.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Через полтора месяца он был обвенчан\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"This is not represented as a reflexive affective outburst. Pierre deliberately recalls and supplies the conventional words expected in the situation, and their poor, embarrassing delivery further marks them as laboured rather than spontaneous discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"The socially scripted function of the expression is adequately represented by its avowal force and its moderate affirmation of the prospective marital bond. The evidence does not establish a further core speech-act mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Hélène's family and guests have effectively treated the pair as engaged, Pierre and Hélène are left together. Following her kiss, Pierre thinks that matters are already settled, recalls the conventional declaration expected on such an occasion, and tells her that he loves her. The words sound poor to him and cause shame.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal avowal moderately affirms Pierre's accepted position as Hélène's prospective husband and the associated marital bond; it is not a separately articulated promise with specified terms. Immediate verbal uptake from Hélène is not supplied after the words, although she has just kissed him, the family has already treated them as engaged, and the supplied scene reports that they marry a month and a half later. The later passage explicitly presents the declaration as a lie and says Pierre believed he had never loved her, while the scene itself records his contemporaneous thought that he did love her; it also clearly depicts desire and attraction. Hence evidence of actual loving affection is mixed, without changing the utterance's avowal or undertaking force.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace, including Pierre Bezukhov's courtship and marriage to Hélène Kuragina.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence supports analysis of this occurrence and includes a later retrospective judgment, but it does not provide an explicit reply from Hélène to the focal words or independently settle Pierre's precise intentions beyond the represented narration and thoughts.\"}"
        }
      ],
